Source: pg-policy
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/rahiakil/pg-policy

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-policy
Architecture: all
Provides: postgresql-pg-policy
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Agent policy language for PostgreSQL PGVERSION
 pg_policy stores and evaluates agent-oriented guardrails, guidance policies,
 session events, and decision logs. It complements PostgreSQL row-level
 security rather than replacing it. The API is installed in the policy schema
 because PostgreSQL reserves schema names beginning with pg_.
